---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
import { dots } from '../../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('AI pilot for our engineering team')}`;
const bodyBg = dots();
---
<Base title="AI adoption for engineering teams" description="A four-week pilot that turns an engineering team's AI tools into closed tickets: a workflow audit, agents on one real repo, and numbers from the team's own tracker.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={11} diagram="assistantsView" eyebrow="Knowledge assistants · Engineering teams" title="AI adoption for engineering teams">
    <p class="lede"><em>"We bought the AI seats and nothing changed."</em> Most teams get Copilot or Claude licenses and a Slack thread of tips. Throughput stays flat because nobody changed the workflow. I changed the workflow for a team on a live finance platform, and ticket throughput rose 65%.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about a pilot</a></p>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="muted">Part of <a href="/knowledge-assistants">Knowledge assistants</a>: the same work, aimed at an engineering team's own code and tickets.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get: a four-week pilot</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Week 1.</strong> I sit in your workflow: repo, tickets, review process, CI. I write down where the time goes.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 2–3.</strong> I set up agents and tooling on one real repo, with your engineers, on real tickets, and I write down the conventions so the gains survive my leaving.</li>
        <li><strong>Week 4.</strong> You get before-and-after numbers from your own tracker and a short list of what to do next.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Good fit if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You have a team of three to thirty engineers and a backlog that keeps growing.</li>
        <li>You've already paid for AI tools and cannot say what changed.</li>
        <li>You want the numbers from your own tracker, not a vendor's slide.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">Four weeks</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about a pilot</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/knowledge-assistants" />
</Base>
